(D1 - Discrepancy 1 repro: LANGUAGE.md:4662 lists `isn't` and `aren't` as
 accepted spellings of `not`. Neither lexes. src/lexer/scan.rs:360 does
 map "isn't" | "aren't" | "doesn't" | "don't" to Token::Not, so the
 intent is in the compiler - but the scanner splits the apostrophe off
 first (it is the possessive marker and the quoted-name delimiter,
 scan.rs:118 and :587), so the contraction never reaches that keyword
 table. `doesn't` and `don't` fail identically and are not documented.
